    {
      "text": "Fearow is recognized by its long neck and elongated beak. They are conveniently shaped for catching prey in soil or water. It deftly moves its long and skinny beak to pluck prey.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fearow is recognized by its long neck and elongated beak. They are conveniently shaped for catching prey in soil or water. It deftly moves its long and skinny beak to pluck prey.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s tough and has excellent stamina. It has no problem flying continuously for a whole day carrying a heavy load.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drawings of a Pokémon resembling Fearow can be seen in murals from deep in ancient history.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carrying food through Fearow’s territory is dangerous. It will snatch the food away from you in a flash!",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "In Alola, fish Pokémon are its prey. It can be seen circling above the ocean searching for food.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Pokémon that dates back many years. If it senses danger, it flies high and away, instantly.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
